# The globe's land texture is DERIVED FROM AN OUTSIDE LAND-COVER MAP, not drawn
# here, and this repository is public. Every other PNG under mod/Resources is
# art this project generated and is committed.
#
# Regenerate it with build/make_globe_texture.py, which also documents where
# the source comes from. The game falls back to the untextured globe without
# it, so a fresh clone still runs.
mod/Resources/Globe/earth.png

# Ten ORIGINAL X-COM tilesets, same reason. Their .MCD is a byte copy of the
# file in the game's own TERRAIN directory and arrived read-only from it; the
# .PCK and .TAB beside each one are this project's 4x re-render of that same
# art, so they are derivative of it rather than new work. Everything in
# mod/TERRAIN with a Joe, Cobra or North-America name is ours and is committed.
#
# MARS is Cydonia's, not Destro's M.A.R.S. - the name collides and the file
# does not.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS: the 4x re-renders are not reproducible from anything in
# build/. render_tileset.py only draws a sheet to look at. A fresh clone can
# rebuild every Joe tileset and none of these ten, so if they are ever lost
# they are re-done by hand.
mod/TERRAIN/BRAIN.*
mod/TERRAIN/MARS.*
mod/TERRAIN/UFO1.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_BASE.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_BITS.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_DISEC2.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_EXT02.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_OPER2.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_PODS.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_WALL02.*
